# local-backend is local only

local-backend mimics Google Cloud on a laptop. It is never deployed.

- Do not add a Dockerfile, container config, Cloud Run/Cloud Functions/App Engine config, Cloud Build file, Terraform, deploy script, or CI deploy workflow under `local-backend/`.
- Mock the cloud resources here: Firestore as SQLite (`data/firestore.sqlite3`), Cloud Storage as files (`data/storage`), Cloud Tasks as the in-process job runner, Firebase Auth as the `X-User-Id` header stub, and the event bus as in-memory WebSocket fan-out.
- Gemini on Vertex (Application Default Credentials), Genkit, and Remotion rendering are allowed. They run on the laptop.
- Business logic stays in `packages/pipeline` and `packages/api`. This folder implements the ports (SQLite, files, in-process jobs, the `X-User-Id` stub, WebSocket) and wires them in `src/index.ts`. HTTP routes are registered by `registerKrayonApi`.
- Cloud-hosted code belongs in `backend/`, not here.
- Keep `logs/app.log` and `logs/app.jsonl`, request ids, redaction, and truncated bodies.

```text
// Bad: a container build for this folder
local-backend/Dockerfile

// Good: the same pipeline, hosted later
backend/
```
